    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match (possible duplicate) rule for owner creation. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* `telephone` is now still created, flagged with `possibleDuplicate: true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate` is `false`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added two persisted columns, `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`), with getters/setters, so the flags survive the create\u2192GET round-trip.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `applyPossibleDuplicate(owner)`, called in `addOwner` right after the hard-duplicate check. It matches existing owners by normalized last name (case/whitespace-insensitive, consistent with the other field comparisons) and equal non-null postcode with a differing telephone, picking the earliest matching owner by id for determinism.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` as read-only properties on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct maps them automatically.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table in each dialect.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS` (the acceptance test `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` is the only runnable test class in the project, and the full `mvn test` run passes).\n\nOne note: this change lives entirely in the v1 controller/OpenAPI path that the acceptance test exercises (`POST /api/owners`, `GET /api/owners/{id}`); I did not touch `OwnerRestControllerV2`, which is unaffected and still compiles.",
